ess schema, locale-driven form), robust currency utility module with zero/3-decimal handling, and global payment method ranking with graceful degradation\n11\t2026-06-21 | answers/08 | wrote 08-observability-analytics.md — 10 answers (7 Core + 3 Deep) covering checkout funnel event taxonomy with typed envelope, three-tier abandonment classification with Beacon API, four-layer PCI sanitization strategy (Sentry beforeSend/Datadog RUM mask/analytics allowlist), custom performance.mark RUM instrumentation for Stripe.js init and Elements mount, real-time success rate dashboard with Datadog monitor YAML, retry effectiveness instrumentation with soft/hard decline segmentation, payment_intent_id risk framework with SHA-256 hashing alternative, full A/B experiment design for load-time vs abandonment causality, 60-second incident detection observability architecture, and deploy-regression diagnostic playbook with Datadog/Sentry/Stripe Dashboard\n12\t2026-06-21 | answers/09 | wrote 09-architecture-provider-abstraction.md — 10 answers (7 Core + 3 Deep) covering IPaymentProvider adapter pattern, PSP SDK normalisation (Stripe/Adyen/Braintree), PSP-agnostic payment method config data model, redirect vs iframe auth flow abstraction, thin-shim vs rich-unified-API tradeoffs, error normalisation to FrontendPaymentError categories, lazy SDK loading with registry + dynamic import, multi-PSP DOM mounting with visibility toggling and event bus, provider failover architecture constraints (pre-created server tokens, double-charge risk, card iframe limitation), and Braintree→Stripe migration playbook (deterministic cohort routing, parallel SDK chunking, cross-provider analytics, migration-complete criteria)\n13\t2026-06-21 | architecture-map | wrote payments-system-frontend-architecture.html — 21 nodes across 7 layers, 38 edges, 5 flow walkthroughs (checkout, decline/retry, 3DS, async payment, PSP failover), 9 sections mapped to answer pages\n14\t2026-06-21 | interview-template | wrote payme